Subject: Fix GH-18743 musl TLSGD register constraint on PHP 8.2

Alpine 3.24 binutils rejects the PHP 8.2 x86_64 JIT tlsgd assembly because the output constraint is "=a" and GAS requires rdi. The upstream change switches those three constraints to "=D". PHP 8.3 and later already contain this commit, and the 8.2 branch including 8.2.35 does not.

Origin: backport, https://github.com/php/php-src/commit/b3c8afe272a6919248986c703c2e1defc73ff707
Base-Tree: tarball https://www.php.net/distributions/php-8.2.35.tar.xz sha256:5737b98601fe5ab1b8c5db0c82ed3158acb9283ed3081ffe2faffb9ac81455e6
Adaptation: Dropped the NEWS hunk from b3c8afe272a6. The three zend_jit_x86.dasc constraints are the upstream commit unchanged and apply on the 8.2.35 tree with a twelve-line context offset.
Verify: test ext/opcache/jit/zend_jit_x86.dasc
Drop-When: upstream >= 8.3.0

diff --git a/ext/opcache/jit/zend_jit_x86.dasc b/ext/opcache/jit/zend_jit_x86.dasc
index 1f1abb59a1c2..7061f6b2b73a 100644
--- a/ext/opcache/jit/zend_jit_x86.dasc
+++ b/ext/opcache/jit/zend_jit_x86.dasc
@@ -2910,7 +2910,7 @@ static int zend_jit_setup(void)
 
 		__asm__(
 			"leaq _tsrm_ls_cache@tlsgd(%%rip), %0\n"
-			: "=a" (ti));
+			: "=D" (ti));
 		tsrm_tls_offset = ti[1];
 		tsrm_tls_index = ti[0] * 8;
 #elif defined(__FreeBSD__)
@@ -2918,7 +2918,7 @@ static int zend_jit_setup(void)
 
 		__asm__(
 			"leaq _tsrm_ls_cache@tlsgd(%%rip), %0\n"
-			: "=a" (ti));
+			: "=D" (ti));
 		tsrm_tls_offset = ti[1];
 		/* Index is offset by 1 on FreeBSD (https://github.com/freebsd/freebsd-src/blob/bf56e8b9c8639ac4447d223b83cdc128107cc3cd/libexec/rtld-elf/rtld.c#L5260) */
 		tsrm_tls_index = (ti[0] + 1) * 8;
@@ -2927,7 +2927,7 @@ static int zend_jit_setup(void)
 
 		__asm__(
 			"leaq _tsrm_ls_cache@tlsgd(%%rip), %0\n"
-			: "=a" (ti));
+			: "=D" (ti));
 		tsrm_tls_offset = ti[1];
 		tsrm_tls_index = ti[0] * 16;
 #endif
